# Copy this file to .env and fill in ONE of the two options below.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# .env is gitignored and must never be committed. Nothing in this repo ever
# prints, logs, or echoes the key's value — including the AWS deployment
# scripts, which redact it in dry-run output.
#
# You do NOT need any of this to run the test suite. All 504 offline tests
# pass with no credentials and no network. Credentials are only needed to
# make real model calls (CLI runs, the web UIs, the Streamlit demos).

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Option A — call Anthropic's API directly (simplest for local dev and demos)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Option B — use Amazon Bedrock instead (leave ANTHROPIC_API_KEY blank)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Configure AWS credentials the normal way — environment variables,
# ~/.aws/credentials, or an assumed role — and each project picks Bedrock
# automatically when no Anthropic key is present. AgentCore deployments
# always use this path.
#
# AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
# AWS_REGION=us-west-2

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional per-project overrides
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Each project selects its provider independently, so you can point one at
# Bedrock and another at Anthropic in the same checkout. Set the provider
# explicitly to override the auto-detection above.
#
# BIDWRIGHT_MODEL_PROVIDER=anthropic      # or "bedrock"
# CLAIMCLARITY_MODEL_PROVIDER=anthropic
# GLACIERWATCH_MODEL_PROVIDER=anthropic
# TRINETRA_MODEL_PROVIDER=anthropic
#
# ...and to pin a specific model per project:
#
# BIDWRIGHT_MODEL_ID=claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929
# CLAIMCLARITY_MODEL_ID=claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929
# GLACIERWATCH_MODEL_ID=claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929
# TRINETRA_MODEL_ID=claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional — Trinetra's A2A agent server (see TRINETRA.md's A2A section)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Only needed when running server_trinetra_a2a.py. TRINETRA_A2A_PUBLIC_URL is
# the address peers should call back on; behind a load balancer a container
# cannot know it, so it has to be supplied. Unset is fine locally.
#
# TRINETRA_A2A_HOST=127.0.0.1
# TRINETRA_A2A_PORT=9100
# TRINETRA_A2A_PUBLIC_URL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional — opt-in live integration tests (these DO cost money)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Three tests are skipped by default because they make real model calls.
# Enable them individually; see TESTING.md.
#
# BIDWRIGHT_RUN_INTEGRATION=1
# CLAIMCLARITY_RUN_INTEGRATION=1
# GLACIERWATCH_RUN_INTEGRATION=1
